The probe uses old syntax supported in this tree and omits T2 extraction. The shown Never is the existing monomorphic lower-bound display, not evidence that the encode parameter is closed. T2 acceptance is inferred from the proposed rules, not run.

Code trace: make's generalized result is Codec(a,b); id has a variable result. call() returns ft.ret.clone() at infer.rs:1353 when the callee is a function. The instantiated id result is therefore a weak variable holding Codec(d,e) as a lower bound. Non-direct size remains Scheme::mono(t) at infer.rs:323. Decode d has Int below; encode e only needs to be below Int. P4 can constrain the outer variable's shape while R4 fixes d and skips e. R5 only records a closed_type for fully fixed variables, and supplies no reusable partial-skeleton status. An importing P4 read traversing the weak outer variable fails its ownership/full-fixation condition despite R3's promise to allow the already fixed component.
